cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below and this software record."
type: software
title: "Micromagnetic GNN: code for Graph Neural Networks for Explainable and Uncertainty-Aware Design of Permanent-Magnet Microstructures"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/heisammoustafa/micromagnetic-gnn"
abstract: >-
  Edge-centric graph neural network with global state updates, trained as a
  surrogate for micromagnetic simulation of Nd2Fe14B polycrystalline
  microstructures. It predicts the coercive field, the maximum energy product
  and the per-grain nucleation field from grain-graph representations, with
  Monte Carlo dropout and deep-ensemble uncertainty quantification and
  gradient-based explanations. The repository contains the package, the
  training pipelines, the trained model checkpoints and the scripts that
  generate the figures of the paper. The training data and the paper figures
  are archived in a separate Zenodo record.
keywords:
  - graph neural network
  - micromagnetics
  - permanent magnets
  - Nd2Fe14B
  - uncertainty quantification
  - explainable machine learning
